Separate your calculations from presentation. I usually put my input and processing steps into an R file. Then I create an R file where I setup any calculation parameters, source the calculations file, and use save.image() to store the results. Then I create the Rnw file that re-loads any needed libraries and uses the load() function to pull the results into memory, and the rest of the Rnw file renders the output. As I refine my calculations I move more and more of them into functions that produce objects and fewer global variables are used. This allows me to store result sets into lists and use knitr templates to render multiple calculation cases.

